      "customfield_10300" : "{}",
      "description" : {
         "content" : [
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "POSSIBLE THREAD ABORT BUG. We send signal, and in that signal handler, set TLS (thread local storage) flag, but the hander may not complete before execution of EINTR happens. Search this. We assume it completes before eintr, but I’m not sure that’s true. It could hit mutex locks etc.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "IN FACT – because of this – REDO CODE IN ",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "SignalHandlerRegistry::FirstPassSignalHandler_",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "To be EVEN MORE CONSERVATIVE – storing JUST THE MINMAL PRECOMPUITED CRAP needs to run, and then retest and assure I made shutdown/restart behavior in BLKQCL-Controller no worse!",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            }
         ],
         "type" : "doc",
         "version" : 1
      },
